              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "nyama-choma"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Nyama Choma"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " translates from Swahili as roasted meat. In Kenya, it is less a recipe and more a ritual. The meat cooks slowly over charcoal until the outside chars and the inside stays juicy. This griddle-pan version brings that flavour indoors."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beef sirloin works well here in place of the traditional goat. Cut into large chunks and thread onto skewers for even cooking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "beef-sirloin",
              "amount": 700,
