      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the garlic, lemon juice, chilli flakes, cumin and oil in a bowl. Add the beef chunks and toss to coat. Leave at room temperature for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Thread the beef onto metal skewers. Pack the pieces close together."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the griddle pan over high heat for 3 minutes until very hot. Place the skewers on the griddle and cook for 5 minutes without moving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn and cook for another 5 minutes. Reduce the heat to medium and continue turning every 5 minutes for a total of 25 to 30 minutes, until the outside is charred and the centre is cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest for 5 minutes before sliding off the skewers. Serve with ugali, braised kale, or a simple tomato and onion salad."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Meat is dry after grilling"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Nyama Choma is meant to be slightly dry on the outside. Use larger chunks so the centre stays moist. Do not overcook beyond 30 minutes for sirloin."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Meat is not charring on the griddle"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The pan needs to be very hot before the meat goes on. Press the skewers down firmly onto the ridges. Do not move them for the first 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Inside is pink after the full cooking time"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cut a piece open to check. If pink, slide the chunks off the skewers and finish in a hot oven at 200C for 8 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Nyama Choma is sold at roadside stands called choma joints across Kenya. It is the food of gatherings, celebrations, and Sunday afternoons. Friends share whole roasted joints pulled apart by hand. In Nairobi, entire restaurants serve nothing else. Goat is the most traditional meat, but beef and chicken are common today."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
